import ../../site/games/river/controller.dl
import site_fixture.dl
import ../../site/games/river/rendering.dl

set painter to (the function named "paint the website river $") as a pointer
require condition (painter != (0 as a pointer)) reporting "The River surface has no painter"

set instance to an instance of website fixture
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
initialize the website river in (the address of state)
require condition ((the value of "River rescue hint" in (the address of instance)) = -1) reporting "A coding hint was visible before it was requested"
set state's river's artwork to 1
set state's river's audio's status to 2
require condition ((the UI element (the control labeled "River play" in (the address of instance)) is enabled in (the address of instance)) = false) reporting "A game without a trace allowed Replay"
require condition (follow website river action (the string form of "action:river") in (the address of state)) reporting "The challenge action was not registered"
require condition ((the value of "Challenge views" in (the address of instance)) = 1) reporting "Opening the river did not select its UI"
set the text of "River source" in (the address of instance) to "get the sheep in the boat\nrow to the other side"
set editor to the UI source editor labeled "River source" in (state's language)
set main to editor's document
set helper to a UI source document named "helper.dl" at "file:///lib/helper.dl" containing "An imported definition" in (main's project)
show UI source document helper in editor in (the address of view)
set {main state} to the UI text state for main in editor in (the address of instance)
mark UI text (main state's text) in layer "search" at priority 20 in main state
add UI text mark (UI ink 210 170 55) from 0 to 3 with opacity 70 in layer "search" in main state
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-step") in (the address of state)
set index to the website program for source "River source"
set program to state's programs + index
require condition ((program's phase = 1) and (state's river's stepping)) reporting "Step without a trace did not compile for one instruction"
require condition ((the UI element (the control labeled "One instruction" in (the address of instance)) is enabled in (the address of instance)) = false) reporting "A compilation left Step enabled"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "status" is 0, JSON number "artifact" is 42, JSON number "milliseconds" is 0.5]
receive website compilation reply for index in (the address of state)
free reply
set program's output to "DYNLEX|TRACE|2|0|2|25|-1\nRIVER|COMMAND|LOAD|SHEEP\nRIVER|ACTION|LOAD|SHEEP\nDYNLEX|TRACE|3|0|3|21|-1\nRIVER|COMMAND|CROSS\nRIVER|ACTION|CROSS|FAR\n"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "milliseconds" is 1]
receive website execution reply for index in (the address of state)
free reply
require condition ((program's phase = 3) and (state's river's playing)) reporting "A valid trace did not begin its presentation"
set execution to the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state
require condition (execution != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "The executing instruction has no annotation layer"
set annotation to execution's marks
require condition ((the UI value for (editor's node) in (the address of instance))'s mark layers = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "Executing the main program marked the displayed imported file."
require condition ((annotation != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text mark)) and (annotation's start = 0)) reporting "The executing instruction was not marked in its source"
advance website river playback (the address of (state's river)) by 0.56
require condition ((state's river's paused) and (state's river's scene's cargo = 1)) reporting "The requested first step did not stop after loading"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-play") in (the address of state)
advance website river playback (the address of (state's river)) by 1.0
require condition ((state's river's playing = false) and (state's river's scene's bank = 1)) reporting "Play did not finish the retained trace"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-speed") in (the address of state)
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-speed") in (the address of state)
require condition (state's river's speed = 4) reporting "Speed did not cycle to four times"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-reset") in (the address of state)
require condition ((state's river's scene's bank = 0) and (state's river's trace's count = 2)) reporting "Reset did not retain a replayable plan"
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "River world state" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "THE RIVER / WAITING FOR A PLAN") reporting "Reset still described the previous replay as ended"
require condition ((the UI text mark layer named "search" in main state)'s marks' end = 3) reporting "Resetting execution also cleared independent search marks"
require condition ((the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state) = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "Resetting execution retained its annotation layer"
run website program index in (the address of state)
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "status" is 0, JSON number "artifact" is 43, JSON number "milliseconds" is 0.5]
receive website compilation reply for index in (the address of state)
free reply
set program's output to "RIVER|COMMAND|CROSS\nRIVER|ACTION|CROSS|FAR\nRIVER|DANGER|WOLF|SHEEP\nRIVER|ERROR|The wolf ate the sheep.\n"
set reply to a JSON object containing [JSON number "milliseconds" is 1]
receive website execution reply for index in (the address of state)
free reply
advance website river playback (the address of (state's river)) by 0.625
refresh website river controls in (the address of state)
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "River diagnostics" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "The wolf ate the sheep.") reporting "A failed game did not show its diagnostic after the danger animation"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-hint-rescue") in (the address of state)
require condition ((the value of "River rescue hint" in (the address of instance)) = 0) reporting "A coding hint did not open"
ignore follow website river action (the string form of "action:river-hint-rescue") in (the address of state)
require condition ((the value of "River rescue hint" in (the address of instance)) = -1) reporting "A coding hint did not close"
notice website river source edit (the address of instance)
require condition ((state's river's trace's count = 0) and (state's river's playing = false)) reporting "Editing retained a stale replay"
free website river trace the address of (state's river's trace)
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
free state's river's coding
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close the address of instance
print line "River controls select the challenge, compile a single step, replay, change speed, reset, reveal hints and clear stale edits."
